---
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import SectionHeading from "../components/SectionHeading.astro";
---

<Section tone="ink" width="narrow" labelledby="faq-title">
  <SectionHeading eyebrow="Questions" title="Before you try it" id="faq-title" />
  <div class="faq">
    <details>
      <summary><span class="question">Will one machine handle my traffic?</span></summary>
      <p class="muted">cetra is built for analytical queries over many spans. Recent spans stay in memory; older ones go to compressed columnar files that queries scan in parallel, on local disk or in S3. We will publish benchmarks with their method.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary><span class="question">Is one binary a toy?</span></summary>
      <p class="muted">No. cetra has organizations and projects, roles, OpenID Connect sign-in, API keys, LLM judges, annotation queues, datasets, experiments, prompts and a playground, issue detection, alerts, an AI assistant, a SQL console and an MCP server. One binary is how it is packaged, not a limit on what it does.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary><span class="question">What if the project stops?</span></summary>
      <p class="muted">The core is MIT-licensed, and your traces are Parquet files on your disk that you can read without cetra.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary><span class="question">Cloud or self-hosted?</span></summary>
      <p class="muted">Self-host when traces must stay in your infrastructure, or when you don't want a usage bill. Use cetra Cloud when you don't want to run anything. The software is the same.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary><span class="question">Which features are on the Free plan?</span></summary>
      <p class="muted">All of the product: prompts, the playground, annotation queues, issues, the assistant, evaluations and alerts, with limits on how many you set up. Features that call an LLM use your own LLM connection, so your provider bills those tokens. Self-hosted cetra has all of them with no limits. Single sign-on and project roles are the paid Teams add-on.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary><span class="question">Which frameworks work?</span></summary>
      <p class="muted">Anything that sends OpenTelemetry, with helpers for OpenAI, Anthropic, LangChain, LlamaIndex, the Vercel AI SDK, the OpenAI Agents SDK and more. <a href="/docs/integrations/">See the integrations</a></p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary><span class="question">Can it trace my coding agents?</span></summary>
      <p class="muted">Yes. Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI and GitHub Copilot send their traces to cetra; for the first three, one setup command does it (Codex also asks you to trust its hook once). You see API-equivalent cost per person, and per repository and branch where the agent reports them. <a href="/docs/integrations/claude-code/">Set up Claude Code</a></p>
    </details>
  </div>
</Section>

<style>
  .faq {
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
  }
  details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-block: var(--space-4);
  }
  summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    list-style: none;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  .question {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
  }
  /* The marker is decoration: its text is empty for screen readers. */
  summary::after {
    content: "+" / "";
    flex: none;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  details[open] summary::after {
    content: "−" / "";
  }
  details p {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }
</style>
